<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roman von Ungern-Sternberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1885">1885</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Baron Ungern</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roman von Ungern-Sternberg was a Baltic German nobleman and White Russian general in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>. His Asiatic Cavalry Division drove the Chinese out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulaanbaatar">Urga</a> in February 1921 and restored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogd-khan">Bogd Khan</a>, while he ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> with notorious brutality. Defeated by Mongolian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> forces later that year, he was captured and executed by the Bolsheviks in September 1921.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roman-von-ungern-sternberg.jpg" alt="Roman von Ungern-Sternberg" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_Ungern_von_Sternberg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
